1
00:00:00,090 --> 00:00:02,060
[Disclaimer: Characters, locations,
and all depicted events are fictional

2
00:00:02,090 --> 00:00:04,140
and for entertainment purposes only;
viewer discretion is advised]

3
00:00:16,180 --> 00:00:17,100
I'm sorry, Pai.

4
00:00:17,120 --> 00:00:19,120
Wan, it's been so many takes.

5
00:00:19,440 --> 00:00:21,080
Focus only on the person
you're acting with.

6
00:00:21,220 --> 00:00:22,280
Only look at me.

7
00:00:22,630 --> 00:00:23,560
Only listen to me.

8
00:00:24,040 --> 00:00:24,960
Stay with me.

9
00:00:26,520 --> 00:00:29,540
What are your feelings toward Third?

10
00:00:29,560 --> 00:00:30,660
Is it still the same?

11
00:00:31,260 --> 00:00:33,120
Try to keep your distance from him.

12
00:00:33,520 --> 00:00:34,760
- Whoa!
- Third!

13
00:00:35,050 --> 00:00:35,580
Wan!

14
00:00:35,600 --> 00:00:36,300
You hit him for real?

15
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:37,560
I'm sorry.

16
00:00:37,900 --> 00:00:39,360
Chew me out however you want.

17
00:00:40,680 --> 00:00:41,720
I'm here to take responsibility.

18
00:00:42,520 --> 00:00:43,940
Were you being gaslit?

19
00:00:43,960 --> 00:00:45,000
And you still believed that?

20
00:00:45,760 --> 00:00:46,540
I don't know.

21
00:00:47,270 --> 00:00:48,600
Still deciding.

22
00:00:48,910 --> 00:00:50,930
Then, I'll give you as much time as you need

23
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:52,870
because you...

24
00:00:55,760 --> 00:00:58,300
are stuck with me for a long time.

25
00:01:26,720 --> 00:01:28,200
Ugh!

26
00:01:29,360 --> 00:01:30,950
Am I your bestie or something?!

27
00:01:31,430 --> 00:01:33,000
What the heck are you doing?

28
00:01:34,880 --> 00:01:35,920
What did I do?

29
00:01:42,200 --> 00:01:43,640
Right, don't you have a schedule today?

30
00:01:45,560 --> 00:01:46,580
I don't.

31
00:01:46,720 --> 00:01:48,440
Cher told me to take a break.

32
00:01:49,280 --> 00:01:51,039
Look what I've gotta do here.

33
00:01:53,500 --> 00:01:54,920
Next time, if you're not
willing to be here,

34
00:01:55,830 --> 00:01:56,840
you don't have to come.

35
00:01:57,620 --> 00:01:59,039
Hey... no.

36
00:02:00,320 --> 00:02:02,360
I honestly came to apologize.

37
00:02:15,920 --> 00:02:17,020
Have you left yet, Third?

38
00:02:17,180 --> 00:02:18,450
We're meeting at 1 P.M.

39
00:02:19,160 --> 00:02:20,200
I'm heading out.

40
00:02:24,079 --> 00:02:25,120
Want me to give you a ride?

41
00:02:26,250 --> 00:02:27,360
I'd probably still make it in time.

42
00:02:27,700 --> 00:02:28,530
It's fine.

43
00:02:28,550 --> 00:02:30,050
I rode my motorcycle here.

44
00:02:30,160 --> 00:02:31,440
What's on your schedule?

45
00:02:32,280 --> 00:02:33,880
How can you still call yourself a Nine fan?

46
00:02:35,970 --> 00:02:38,040
How come you don't know
your bias's public schedule?

47
00:02:42,340 --> 00:02:43,160
Let's go.

48
00:02:44,380 --> 00:02:45,620
Or maybe...

49
00:02:48,760 --> 00:02:50,320
you'd rather wait for me here?

50
00:02:52,140 --> 00:02:53,470
Whoever wants to stay can stay.

51
00:02:53,710 --> 00:02:54,570
I'm not staying.

52
00:02:55,190 --> 00:02:56,040
Peace out...

53
00:04:20,959 --> 00:04:23,120
♫I'm just a fanboy♫

54
00:04:24,000 --> 00:04:26,120
[Mr. Fanboy Series]

55
00:04:26,160 --> 00:04:28,780
[Episode 5: "Now It Makes Sense"]

56
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:31,080
[SOUP]

57
00:04:44,320 --> 00:04:45,260
Hello, hello.

58
00:04:45,280 --> 00:04:46,170
Hello, hello.

59
00:04:46,190 --> 00:04:47,090
Please make way for them.

60
00:04:47,180 --> 00:04:48,130
Thank you.

61
00:04:49,950 --> 00:04:50,890
- Hello, Nine.
- Oops?

62
00:04:50,909 --> 00:04:52,250
You're Ball, right?

63
00:04:52,280 --> 00:04:53,360
- I thought that was about the World Cup.
- Force of habit.

64
00:04:53,390 --> 00:04:54,240
Hello.

65
00:04:58,850 --> 00:04:59,580
Right, hello.

66
00:04:59,600 --> 00:05:00,460
Let's do an interview, shall we?

67
00:05:00,480 --> 00:05:01,030
Of course.

68
00:05:01,050 --> 00:05:01,550
Absolutely.

69
00:05:01,570 --> 00:05:03,140
- Ball, right?
- Be right back.

70
00:05:03,160 --> 00:05:04,780
- Ballie!
- Right, you're Ballie.

71
00:05:04,800 --> 00:05:05,940
Thank you.

72
00:05:09,040 --> 00:05:09,740
Ooh...

73
00:05:11,630 --> 00:05:12,450
I'm sorry.

74
00:05:12,680 --> 00:05:13,920
You're good.

75
00:05:15,810 --> 00:05:16,410
Uh...

76
00:05:16,430 --> 00:05:17,520
excuse me,

77
00:05:18,050 --> 00:05:20,120
have we met at other events before?

78
00:05:20,350 --> 00:05:21,130
Uh...

79
00:05:21,740 --> 00:05:23,510
maybe we have.

80
00:05:24,310 --> 00:05:27,090
I come to events like this quite often.

81
00:05:27,120 --> 00:05:28,790
But you sound so familiar.

82
00:05:28,810 --> 00:05:30,440
You sound so much like Wan.

83
00:05:30,610 --> 00:05:31,750
No... I'm not him.

84
00:05:31,770 --> 00:05:32,700
I'm not.

85
00:05:33,040 --> 00:05:33,860
Uh...

86
00:05:33,880 --> 00:05:35,250
Please excuse me.

87
00:05:35,270 --> 00:05:36,030
Uh...

88
00:05:42,930 --> 00:05:43,530
Girl...

89
00:05:43,550 --> 00:05:45,370
- What?
- I think this is Wan.

90
00:05:46,640 --> 00:05:47,640
It's definitely him.

91
00:05:47,659 --> 00:05:48,220
Don't you think?

92
00:05:48,240 --> 00:05:48,960
Huh?

93
00:05:49,200 --> 00:05:50,450
And why would he be here?

94
00:05:50,630 --> 00:05:52,159
If he comes, he's getting a piece of me

95
00:05:52,180 --> 00:05:53,560
for punching my baby boy in the mouth.

96
00:05:56,580 --> 00:05:59,800
Then, allow me to ask about
the hottest topic right now.

97
00:06:00,010 --> 00:06:02,960
Recently, some news
has surfaced that you and Wan

98
00:06:02,980 --> 00:06:04,560
got so immersed in your roles

99
00:06:04,780 --> 00:06:07,260
that you ended up
getting into a real fight on set.

100
00:06:08,860 --> 00:06:09,240
Right,

101
00:06:09,260 --> 00:06:10,900
let me make this clear.

102
00:06:11,800 --> 00:06:13,100
Wan and I were not fighting.

103
00:06:14,090 --> 00:06:16,000
It was one of the scenes in the pilot.

104
00:06:16,040 --> 00:06:17,720
And him punching me

105
00:06:17,890 --> 00:06:20,320
was an accident on set,

106
00:06:20,690 --> 00:06:22,920
and the producer has released
a statement to clarify it.

107
00:06:23,390 --> 00:06:24,130
Actually,

108
00:06:24,150 --> 00:06:25,480
I wasn't there when it happened,

109
00:06:25,500 --> 00:06:27,870
but when I found out

110
00:06:27,890 --> 00:06:29,530
about a miscue on set,

111
00:06:29,550 --> 00:06:30,970
I was a little shocked.

112
00:06:30,990 --> 00:06:33,060
So I asked Third if he was alright,

113
00:06:33,080 --> 00:06:34,430
but he said he was fine,

114
00:06:34,450 --> 00:06:36,070
just a small wound
at the corner of his mouth.

115
00:06:36,090 --> 00:06:36,920
Huh?!

116
00:06:37,090 --> 00:06:38,330
A wound at the corner of his mouth?!

117
00:06:38,360 --> 00:06:38,920
Exactly.

118
00:06:38,940 --> 00:06:40,120
He had a wound?

119
00:06:40,210 --> 00:06:41,560
Oh, just a tiny one.

120
00:06:41,990 --> 00:06:42,430
Yeah,

121
00:06:42,450 --> 00:06:44,020
but I treated his wound

122
00:06:44,040 --> 00:06:45,440
and took him home.

123
00:06:45,700 --> 00:06:47,360
You took him home?!

124
00:06:47,770 --> 00:06:48,250
Yes,

125
00:06:48,270 --> 00:06:49,659
I did take him home.

126
00:06:53,150 --> 00:06:54,520
Uh, anyway...

127
00:06:54,540 --> 00:06:56,030
I do think

128
00:06:56,050 --> 00:06:57,300
it was an honest mistake

129
00:06:57,320 --> 00:06:58,540
because Wan is still so new.

130
00:06:58,560 --> 00:06:59,440
That's why

131
00:06:59,460 --> 00:07:01,310
the accident happened on set,

132
00:07:01,330 --> 00:07:03,090
as the producer explained in the statement.

133
00:07:03,110 --> 00:07:03,910
Mm...

134
00:07:03,930 --> 00:07:05,670
but people on social media

135
00:07:05,690 --> 00:07:08,080
seem to be really upset with Wan.

136
00:07:10,100 --> 00:07:11,070
I think that people on X

137
00:07:11,090 --> 00:07:12,430
have gotten it so wrong

138
00:07:14,160 --> 00:07:15,600
without knowing the whole truth.

139
00:07:16,180 --> 00:07:18,050
I don't think this is fair to Wan.

140
00:07:18,950 --> 00:07:20,970
And everyone working behind the scenes

141
00:07:21,020 --> 00:07:22,440
has been working so hard.

142
00:07:22,770 --> 00:07:24,580
Also, Wan and I are getting along well.

143
00:07:26,790 --> 00:07:27,240
Uh...

144
00:07:27,410 --> 00:07:27,990
that's right.

145
00:07:28,020 --> 00:07:29,000
So, uh...

146
00:07:29,080 --> 00:07:30,880
Anyway, everyone,

147
00:07:30,930 --> 00:07:32,850
please understand.

148
00:07:32,870 --> 00:07:33,520
Lastly,

149
00:07:33,540 --> 00:07:36,510
please look forward to our series,

150
00:07:36,530 --> 00:07:37,909
'The Deep Between Us.'

151
00:07:37,930 --> 00:07:40,880
Right now, the pilot is about to launch.

152
00:07:41,150 --> 00:07:42,110
I'm so excited,

153
00:07:42,130 --> 00:07:44,040
and you are too, right?

154
00:07:44,230 --> 00:07:45,440
Anyway...

155
00:07:45,510 --> 00:07:47,580
please give us your support.

156
00:07:47,610 --> 00:07:49,260
Yes, please stay tuned.

157
00:07:49,280 --> 00:07:50,290
Please do.

158
00:07:51,280 --> 00:07:52,560
- Thank you.
- Please stay tuned.

159
00:07:52,580 --> 00:07:54,100
Yes, thank you.

160
00:07:54,990 --> 00:07:56,159
Sunny, have you seen this?

161
00:07:56,250 --> 00:07:57,590
"Third's betraying Nine.

162
00:07:57,610 --> 00:07:59,710
He's so disrespectful to his own partner.

163
00:07:59,920 --> 00:08:01,440
He doesn't even thank Nine.

164
00:08:01,710 --> 00:08:02,800
Nine seems so worried about Third,

165
00:08:02,820 --> 00:08:04,650
but all he does is protect
someone who hurts him.

166
00:08:04,670 --> 00:08:06,260
How could he forget the person beside him?

167
00:08:06,570 --> 00:08:07,540
What an awful move.

168
00:08:07,560 --> 00:08:08,800
So disrespectful to Nine.

169
00:08:08,890 --> 00:08:10,730
More importantly,
the cute moments are nonexistent.

170
00:08:10,750 --> 00:08:12,150
That man spits those out
when he's being fed."

171
00:08:15,380 --> 00:08:17,430
"See his eyes
when he's talking about Wan?

172
00:08:17,450 --> 00:08:18,840
With that sweet, sweet look,

173
00:08:18,940 --> 00:08:20,400
why don't you change
your partner already, you bastard?!"

174
00:08:25,110 --> 00:08:25,660
Ooh...

175
00:08:26,680 --> 00:08:27,640
That "bastard" part wasn't there.

176
00:08:28,100 --> 00:08:29,080
I added it.

177
00:08:32,980 --> 00:08:33,659
Mama,

178
00:08:34,659 --> 00:08:36,159
let's find something sweet to eat.

179
00:08:37,690 --> 00:08:39,990
How does one turn a crisis
into an even more fucked-up crisis?

180
00:08:41,840 --> 00:08:43,049
With utter stupidity, I guess.

181
00:08:44,100 --> 00:08:45,400
Your mom's gonna come chew your ass out,

182
00:08:45,710 --> 00:08:46,580
Richie Rich.

183
00:08:50,890 --> 00:08:52,150
Don't listen too much to what he says.

184
00:08:52,830 --> 00:08:53,570
Let it go.

185
00:08:54,450 --> 00:08:56,430
Go get changed now so you can go home.

186
00:09:23,760 --> 00:09:24,630
Wan.

187
00:09:50,370 --> 00:09:51,340
Hey!

188
00:09:51,830 --> 00:09:52,980
Don't mess with my stuff!

189
00:09:53,000 --> 00:09:53,770
Are you nuts?

190
00:09:53,790 --> 00:09:55,220
Aren't you afraid you'll get caught?

191
00:09:57,440 --> 00:09:59,730
You realize you can't go
support your bias like you did, right?

192
00:10:01,180 --> 00:10:02,110
I do...

193
00:10:03,040 --> 00:10:04,790
I just happened to pass by.

194
00:10:04,810 --> 00:10:06,610
I'm serious, Wan.

195
00:10:06,640 --> 00:10:08,240
Even if your fanbase
is completely abandoned

196
00:10:08,260 --> 00:10:09,600
and has no photos of Nine to post,

197
00:10:09,620 --> 00:10:11,240
you can't go
support your bias like you did.

198
00:10:14,680 --> 00:10:15,600
I'm saying this

199
00:10:15,620 --> 00:10:16,820
because I'm worried.

200
00:10:17,040 --> 00:10:18,120
What?!

201
00:10:18,580 --> 00:10:19,990
You're already involved in a drama.

202
00:10:20,010 --> 00:10:22,640
Do you even know
you're about to be dragged into another one?

203
00:10:29,320 --> 00:10:30,020
Here.

204
00:10:34,310 --> 00:10:35,200
I think that people on X

205
00:10:35,230 --> 00:10:36,380
have gotten it so wrong...

206
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:37,290
[Anyone else feel that tension?]

207
00:10:37,310 --> 00:10:38,700
without knowing the whole truth.

208
00:10:39,270 --> 00:10:41,160
I don't think this is fair to Wan.

209
00:10:41,680 --> 00:10:43,580
And everyone working behind the scenes...

210
00:10:44,000 --> 00:10:46,280
Third really put you under fire.

211
00:10:51,170 --> 00:10:52,680
And what are the comments saying?

212
00:10:53,040 --> 00:10:55,080
Nine's fans
are cussing Third out like crazy.

213
00:11:01,520 --> 00:11:02,910
And there's one more thing.

214
00:11:03,710 --> 00:11:05,960
Fans have started
a ThirdWan fanbase on X.

215
00:11:07,450 --> 00:11:08,200
But why?

216
00:11:08,670 --> 00:11:10,460
Well, when Third was talking about you,

217
00:11:10,610 --> 00:11:12,280
he was grinning from ear to ear.

218
00:11:12,570 --> 00:11:13,390
There's chemistry;

219
00:11:13,410 --> 00:11:14,640
how could they resist shipping?

220
00:11:15,120 --> 00:11:16,410
You're screwed, dude.

221
00:11:19,720 --> 00:11:22,390
Ugh...

222
00:11:23,830 --> 00:11:25,570
Nine's gonna be so mad at me...

223
00:11:26,620 --> 00:11:28,880
Since news has spread about the miscue

224
00:11:28,900 --> 00:11:29,990
on the set of The Deep Between Us,

225
00:11:30,940 --> 00:11:33,040
it has sparked a backlash against Wan.

226
00:11:34,240 --> 00:11:36,020
Your companies and I have discussed it

227
00:11:36,040 --> 00:11:37,480
and decided that...

228
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:39,450
for the sake of our set's image,

229
00:11:39,470 --> 00:11:41,520
we're gonna have the cast members

230
00:11:41,760 --> 00:11:42,720
spend some time...

231
00:11:42,740 --> 00:11:44,040
living together.

232
00:11:48,700 --> 00:11:50,880
Won't this affect us when we start filming?

233
00:11:51,040 --> 00:11:52,560
We're doing this before that.

234
00:11:54,160 --> 00:11:55,470
Like I said,

235
00:11:56,030 --> 00:11:57,610
your companies and I

236
00:11:57,630 --> 00:11:59,090
have already decided this.

237
00:11:59,890 --> 00:12:02,510
Not only will it help resolve
the issues with our image,

238
00:12:02,530 --> 00:12:05,640
but it'll also bring you guys closer together
before filming actually begins.

239
00:12:05,760 --> 00:12:06,360
Right,

240
00:12:07,220 --> 00:12:08,140
this time...

241
00:12:09,090 --> 00:12:10,470
I'm not sending any staff with you.

242
00:12:16,080 --> 00:12:17,830
Why isn't that allowed?

243
00:12:18,500 --> 00:12:20,290
Well, I want you guys...

244
00:12:20,310 --> 00:12:21,680
to really spend some time together.

245
00:12:25,140 --> 00:12:26,420
Uh, so what are we doing

246
00:12:26,440 --> 00:12:28,480
on this trip, North?

247
00:12:29,050 --> 00:12:30,040
Since that period

248
00:12:30,060 --> 00:12:31,760
is exactly when we're releasing the pilot,

249
00:12:31,860 --> 00:12:34,080
you'll be filming a reaction video

250
00:12:34,100 --> 00:12:35,600
and some other content for us.

251
00:12:35,650 --> 00:12:37,100
We're keeping the buzz alive.

252
00:12:37,120 --> 00:12:39,280
Once you return, we're holding
a blessing ceremony before filming.

253
00:12:39,580 --> 00:12:40,370
Perfect timing.

254
00:12:44,640 --> 00:12:46,240
We get to spend all day together, Wan.

255
00:12:46,920 --> 00:12:47,920
Are you happy?

256
00:12:48,520 --> 00:12:49,960
Without even entering any lucky draw.

257
00:12:56,380 --> 00:12:57,760
Yes, Nine.

258
00:13:08,830 --> 00:13:10,830
So where are we going?

259
00:13:11,590 --> 00:13:12,880
Khao Yai.

260
00:13:16,450 --> 00:13:18,600
[Present]

261
00:13:19,220 --> 00:13:24,040
[Assumption University's Aquatic Center]

262
00:13:24,600 --> 00:13:28,190
My dream might sound
ordinary to someone else.

263
00:13:29,080 --> 00:13:31,680
But for someone as sickly as me,

264
00:13:32,570 --> 00:13:34,730
this is beyond what
I'd ever dare to dream of.

265
00:13:34,760 --> 00:13:37,880
[His health stands
between him and his dream]

266
00:13:39,250 --> 00:13:40,800
Wow...

267
00:13:49,120 --> 00:13:50,370
Watch where you're going.

268
00:13:50,390 --> 00:13:51,500
You're the new kid, right?

269
00:13:54,190 --> 00:13:55,270
I'm Copter.

270
00:13:56,560 --> 00:13:57,490
Hey, new kid.

271
00:13:57,920 --> 00:13:58,900
Why did you drop out?

272
00:13:58,920 --> 00:14:00,080
My name is Noel.

273
00:14:00,190 --> 00:14:01,120
I didn't ask you that.

274
00:14:01,140 --> 00:14:02,560
Then don't call me "new kid."

275
00:14:04,080 --> 00:14:05,080
[A relationship blooms]

276
00:14:09,600 --> 00:14:10,730
Just hold my hand if you want to.

277
00:14:14,580 --> 00:14:16,600
I haven't set foot here in so long.

278
00:14:17,890 --> 00:14:18,720
Why did you come back?

279
00:14:18,740 --> 00:14:19,960
Why can't I?

280
00:14:20,050 --> 00:14:21,540
This is somewhere I used to be.

281
00:14:21,670 --> 00:14:22,220
I won't let you

282
00:14:22,240 --> 00:14:23,380
be happy, Copter.

283
00:14:23,400 --> 00:14:24,400
[A grudge from the past]

284
00:14:24,570 --> 00:14:25,760
So now you wanna talk?

285
00:14:25,820 --> 00:14:26,760
Leave Noel alone.

286
00:14:27,680 --> 00:14:29,640
Noel, that new special someone of yours?

287
00:14:29,760 --> 00:14:30,840
Don't say I didn't warn you.

288
00:14:31,630 --> 00:14:32,400
Is this...

289
00:14:32,420 --> 00:14:34,650
the promising young shark?

290
00:14:35,260 --> 00:14:36,560
All I can see is a fucking loser.

291
00:14:36,580 --> 00:14:37,800
You hate me

292
00:14:38,630 --> 00:14:40,520
because you were
gonna break up with Bas and fall for me?

293
00:14:40,720 --> 00:14:42,120
[A decision between a dream and...]

294
00:14:42,390 --> 00:14:43,600
Don't focus on anything else.

295
00:14:44,170 --> 00:14:45,680
Just focus on swimming.

296
00:14:46,280 --> 00:14:47,950
Well, that's all I want to focus on,

297
00:14:47,970 --> 00:14:48,520
but...

298
00:14:54,960 --> 00:14:55,960
[This love between us]

299
00:14:56,080 --> 00:14:57,200
It's not like that, Noel.

300
00:14:57,240 --> 00:14:58,640
Then what is it, Copter?

301
00:14:59,060 --> 00:15:00,320
What did you say to Noel?

302
00:15:00,460 --> 00:15:01,220
Are you angry?

303
00:15:01,280 --> 00:15:02,240
Shut up!

304
00:15:02,290 --> 00:15:04,000
I... like you.

305
00:15:08,800 --> 00:15:14,300
[The Deep Between Us]

306
00:15:14,320 --> 00:15:17,320
[Soon]

307
00:15:17,960 --> 00:15:18,840
- Whoa...
- Whoa.

308
00:15:21,880 --> 00:15:23,800
Like, I can't wait for the series.

309
00:15:23,820 --> 00:15:24,810
It looks like fun, right?

310
00:15:24,830 --> 00:15:25,440
Third?

311
00:15:25,640 --> 00:15:26,220
Right,

312
00:15:26,240 --> 00:15:27,620
the series itself is so intense.

313
00:15:27,640 --> 00:15:28,730
Please stay tuned.

314
00:15:30,120 --> 00:15:31,060
I'm also...

315
00:15:31,370 --> 00:15:33,010
feeling excited.

316
00:15:33,030 --> 00:15:35,500
Noel's mommies, please don't get mad.

317
00:15:36,580 --> 00:15:37,510
You were not behaving well.

318
00:15:37,530 --> 00:15:38,670
You're gonna get it, Wan.

319
00:15:39,360 --> 00:15:39,830
Alright,

320
00:15:39,850 --> 00:15:40,980
please look forward to it.

321
00:15:42,050 --> 00:15:43,130
Alright, lastly,

322
00:15:43,150 --> 00:15:44,350
stay tuned for

323
00:15:44,380 --> 00:15:46,600
'The Deep Between Us.'

324
00:15:46,620 --> 00:15:47,820
See you soon.

325
00:15:47,840 --> 00:15:48,870
See you.

326
00:15:48,890 --> 00:15:50,680
- Bye-bye.
- Bye-bye.

327
00:15:51,360 --> 00:15:52,350
Cut...

328
00:15:53,310 --> 00:15:54,190
Good job, boys.

329
00:15:54,670 --> 00:15:56,730
You have one hour to rest.

330
00:16:05,860 --> 00:16:06,590
Wan.

331
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:09,670
I think...

332
00:16:09,690 --> 00:16:10,520
you're gonna blow up.

333
00:16:15,360 --> 00:16:16,340
Mm, I think...

334
00:16:16,360 --> 00:16:18,430
this scene was amazing.

335
00:16:19,390 --> 00:16:20,640
It's work.

336
00:16:21,970 --> 00:16:22,960
But it hurt for real.

337
00:16:24,650 --> 00:16:26,570
That digital footprint
will haunt you for life.

338
00:16:27,050 --> 00:16:28,040
You're in trouble...

339
00:16:28,320 --> 00:16:29,160
What?

340
00:16:29,630 --> 00:16:31,120
I told you I didn't mean to.

341
00:16:36,560 --> 00:16:38,570
Don't overthink that punching scene, Wan.

342
00:16:40,910 --> 00:16:42,860
Everyone craves drama on set.

343
00:16:43,510 --> 00:16:45,220
But I do think it's a win for you.

344
00:16:45,830 --> 00:16:46,720
I'm jelly.

345
00:16:46,980 --> 00:16:47,960
You stand out more than I do.

346
00:16:48,380 --> 00:16:49,320
Not at all.

347
00:16:49,340 --> 00:16:51,280
I definitely don't stand out
more than the lead.

348
00:16:51,840 --> 00:16:52,400
Jeez...

349
00:16:52,420 --> 00:16:53,600
anyone and their mother

350
00:16:53,620 --> 00:16:55,200
wants to see ThirdNine.

351
00:16:57,100 --> 00:16:59,320
You never know, though...

352
00:17:06,280 --> 00:17:07,599
It's showbiz, Wan.

353
00:17:07,619 --> 00:17:09,520
Anything new is always all the rage.

354
00:17:10,730 --> 00:17:11,530
That's true,

355
00:17:12,240 --> 00:17:13,770
'cause how could I compare to you?

356
00:17:37,090 --> 00:17:37,940
Right, guys.

357
00:17:38,040 --> 00:17:39,120
I looked at the trending hashtags.

358
00:17:39,200 --> 00:17:40,220
It made me so sad.

359
00:17:40,420 --> 00:17:41,620
There was no "RenjiWan,"

360
00:17:42,330 --> 00:17:43,720
only "ThirdNine"

361
00:17:47,220 --> 00:17:48,450
and...

362
00:17:49,160 --> 00:17:50,040
"ThirdWan,"

363
00:17:54,650 --> 00:17:56,160
the hashtag that overtook "ThirdNine."

364
00:17:59,480 --> 00:18:00,520
Seriously?

365
00:18:10,740 --> 00:18:12,840
"Girl, ThirdWan is so hot right now."

366
00:18:24,120 --> 00:18:25,420
It's pretty quiet, isn't it?

367
00:18:26,620 --> 00:18:27,710
Wanna play a game?

368
00:18:28,890 --> 00:18:30,240
I'll start.

369
00:18:32,670 --> 00:18:33,810
Let's do hard-hitting questions.

370
00:18:34,470 --> 00:18:35,160
For example...

371
00:18:35,500 --> 00:18:36,210
Nine,

372
00:18:36,230 --> 00:18:39,110
how did you feel
when Wan told you he was your fan?

373
00:18:42,670 --> 00:18:44,060
Honestly, it felt weird

374
00:18:44,080 --> 00:18:46,580
when someone told you
they were a fan of yours during a workshop.

375
00:18:47,490 --> 00:18:48,100
However...

376
00:18:48,120 --> 00:18:49,140
I didn't mind.

377
00:18:51,370 --> 00:18:52,700
I'm sorry, Nine.

378
00:18:52,720 --> 00:18:54,610
I didn't think it through that day.

379
00:18:54,640 --> 00:18:55,850
Hey, it's fine.

380
00:18:56,470 --> 00:18:58,080
You didn't cross the line or anything.

381
00:18:58,450 --> 00:18:59,080
Plus...

382
00:18:59,320 --> 00:19:00,470
you know how to carry yourself.

383
00:19:00,670 --> 00:19:01,320
We're chill.

384
00:19:01,510 --> 00:19:02,200
Alright.

385
00:19:03,520 --> 00:19:06,170
Actually, there was one person
who was displeased.

386
00:19:06,900 --> 00:19:07,940
I remember...

387
00:19:08,250 --> 00:19:09,540
Third asking,

388
00:19:09,560 --> 00:19:11,740
"So people who don't
put in effort deserve a chance?"

389
00:19:14,470 --> 00:19:15,950
You were saying...

390
00:19:17,140 --> 00:19:18,980
you wanted Wan
removed from the project?

391
00:19:25,910 --> 00:19:27,120
Mm... Yeah.

392
00:19:32,370 --> 00:19:33,550
Only then, though.

393
00:19:37,350 --> 00:19:38,040
Then...

394
00:19:38,060 --> 00:19:39,200
Let me ask you, Wan.

395
00:19:40,570 --> 00:19:41,370
Right now,

396
00:19:41,910 --> 00:19:43,230
do you like me

397
00:19:43,580 --> 00:19:45,040
or Third more?

398
00:19:47,850 --> 00:19:49,520
Aren't you afraid of the answer?

399
00:19:50,910 --> 00:19:51,700
Why would I be?

400
00:19:51,720 --> 00:19:53,220
Wan says he's my fan, after all.

401
00:19:55,340 --> 00:19:56,960
Of course, he likes me more.

402
00:20:04,250 --> 00:20:05,000
Am I right?

403
00:20:06,520 --> 00:20:07,060
Yes,

404
00:20:07,080 --> 00:20:08,490
I like you just the same, Nine.

405
00:20:16,390 --> 00:20:17,560
Come to think of it...

406
00:20:18,260 --> 00:20:19,720
you haven't been asked, right, Time?

407
00:20:19,980 --> 00:20:20,910
Can I ask you a question?

408
00:20:20,930 --> 00:20:21,680
Say...

409
00:20:22,170 --> 00:20:23,100
that day,

410
00:20:24,020 --> 00:20:25,640
Renji's acting was atrocious,

411
00:20:27,030 --> 00:20:29,040
but someone pulled some strings
and he got the role.

412
00:20:29,660 --> 00:20:30,720
How does that make you feel?

413
00:20:34,960 --> 00:20:36,200
Nothing, actually.

414
00:20:36,220 --> 00:20:37,550
Right...

415
00:20:38,490 --> 00:20:38,910
that makes sense.

416
00:20:38,930 --> 00:20:39,960
How could you feel anything

417
00:20:39,980 --> 00:20:40,780
when...

418
00:20:41,140 --> 00:20:42,950
you and Renji
already knew each other, right?

419
00:20:57,480 --> 00:20:58,610
Then, I'll go next.

420
00:21:00,530 --> 00:21:01,160
Wan,

421
00:21:01,230 --> 00:21:03,560
any thoughts on those who love
throwing people under the bus?

422
00:21:03,590 --> 00:21:04,760
They play the hero,

423
00:21:04,810 --> 00:21:06,230
pretending to ask for help

424
00:21:06,250 --> 00:21:08,160
when in reality,
they're just a backstabber.

425
00:21:08,490 --> 00:21:10,200
Why do you think they're doing that?

426
00:21:11,780 --> 00:21:12,800
You're asking me?

427
00:21:13,560 --> 00:21:15,240
But I'm not that kind of person.

428
00:21:15,520 --> 00:21:16,320
I know.

429
00:21:16,410 --> 00:21:17,440
You didn't do anything like that.

430
00:21:21,720 --> 00:21:22,950
Wanna point the finger?

431
00:21:29,560 --> 00:21:30,880
Then, let me ask you this.

432
00:21:33,870 --> 00:21:35,760
You weren't cramping that day, were you?

433
00:21:40,440 --> 00:21:41,410
Shit!

434
00:21:42,360 --> 00:21:43,680
That's a hardball question.

435
00:21:43,920 --> 00:21:45,620
It's not. I can answer it.

436
00:21:46,400 --> 00:21:48,480
I asked you to massage my feet that day.

437
00:21:48,500 --> 00:21:49,720
Did I look like I was fine?

438
00:21:51,910 --> 00:21:53,700
Do you think I was gonna kill Wan?

439
00:21:53,720 --> 00:21:54,850
Are you fucking nuts?!

440
00:21:55,470 --> 00:21:56,080
Are you insane?

441
00:21:56,100 --> 00:21:57,280
Why would I kill Wan?

442
00:21:59,960 --> 00:22:01,410
Why would I kill Wan?

443
00:22:14,800 --> 00:22:16,180
No more questions?

444
00:22:29,750 --> 00:22:31,230
Look at the camera. Three, two, one!

445
00:22:31,260 --> 00:22:32,160
Nice.

446
00:22:32,200 --> 00:22:33,260
One more time. Three, two, one!

447
00:22:33,280 --> 00:22:34,670
Hold on just a second. Yeah.

448
00:22:34,690 --> 00:22:35,560
Three, two...

449
00:22:37,480 --> 00:22:38,240
Uh...

450
00:22:38,260 --> 00:22:40,920
Renji, Wan, that's a wrap for you today.

451
00:22:41,050 --> 00:22:43,360
Time, please come on set.

452
00:23:25,180 --> 00:23:26,380
Why are you sitting here all stressed?

453
00:23:29,100 --> 00:23:29,900
Is it about Nine?

454
00:23:31,590 --> 00:23:32,360
Mm.

455
00:23:34,830 --> 00:23:36,810
There must be something I did wrong.

456
00:23:44,150 --> 00:23:45,260
Right!

457
00:23:45,510 --> 00:23:48,100
Maybe it's because
you and I are too close.

458
00:23:50,260 --> 00:23:51,090
I don't think so.

459
00:23:52,110 --> 00:23:53,810
Nine's not that invested in me.

460
00:23:55,530 --> 00:23:57,000
But I don't want you to think that way.

461
00:23:57,850 --> 00:23:59,400
You can like or love him,

462
00:24:00,350 --> 00:24:01,620
but you have to love yourself, too.

463
00:24:05,170 --> 00:24:06,020
How?

464
00:24:09,870 --> 00:24:11,410
I can't give you the answers, either.

465
00:24:18,430 --> 00:24:19,760
You and Nine...

466
00:24:23,660 --> 00:24:25,150
Never mind. I won't ask.

467
00:24:25,840 --> 00:24:26,890
You can ask.

468
00:24:29,810 --> 00:24:30,660
No.

469
00:24:32,810 --> 00:24:33,650
Why not?

470
00:24:34,330 --> 00:24:35,330
Scared of the truth?

471
00:24:44,490 --> 00:24:45,630
I've finished my cues.

472
00:24:46,200 --> 00:24:47,360
I'm heading outside.

473
00:24:47,990 --> 00:24:48,870
Where to?

474
00:24:50,570 --> 00:24:51,920
Just sightseeing around here.

475
00:24:52,130 --> 00:24:53,260
No...

476
00:24:54,660 --> 00:24:55,760
They told us to stay here.

477
00:24:56,660 --> 00:24:58,250
The worst that can happen
is getting chewed out, no?

478
00:24:58,500 --> 00:24:59,320
I'm off.

479
00:24:59,730 --> 00:25:00,570
Hey, wait...

480
00:25:01,510 --> 00:25:02,320
I'm coming with you.

481
00:25:03,870 --> 00:25:05,060
Do you even know where I'm going?

482
00:25:05,880 --> 00:25:06,900
No, so lead the way.

483
00:25:08,170 --> 00:25:09,360
So eager to lead, too.

484
00:25:09,380 --> 00:25:10,050
Ugh...

485
00:25:36,750 --> 00:25:38,190
How did you find a place like this?

486
00:25:44,050 --> 00:25:45,760
I overheard the staff talking.

487
00:25:47,390 --> 00:25:48,720
You're a pretty nosy one.

488
00:25:50,180 --> 00:25:51,080
Totally!

489
00:25:54,180 --> 00:25:54,950
Living in the city,

490
00:25:54,970 --> 00:25:56,440
whenever I feel stressed out,

491
00:25:56,520 --> 00:25:58,520
I go for a motorcycle ride
to feel the breeze on my face.

492
00:25:59,110 --> 00:26:00,490
Though switching to a bicycle

493
00:26:00,510 --> 00:26:01,710
gives me some peace of mind.

494
00:26:03,120 --> 00:26:06,310
To me, the speed
of a bicycle is just right.

495
00:26:06,340 --> 00:26:08,360
You enjoy the ride and the view.

496
00:26:09,280 --> 00:26:10,220
It's nice and relaxing.

497
00:26:18,860 --> 00:26:20,230
I think I'm starting to like it.

498
00:26:30,720 --> 00:26:31,490
Like what?

499
00:26:36,500 --> 00:26:37,250
Everything.

500
00:26:38,990 --> 00:26:39,560
Huh?

501
00:26:46,120 --> 00:26:46,850
Good...

502
00:26:47,660 --> 00:26:49,610
That way, you won't
try to get me fired again.

503
00:27:13,230 --> 00:27:14,700
Never once have I run off like this.

504
00:27:16,110 --> 00:27:17,750
Am I gonna get chewed out
when we get back?

505
00:27:19,460 --> 00:27:21,490
If so, just defend me.

506
00:27:22,130 --> 00:27:24,320
Is this actually your plan?!

507
00:27:24,440 --> 00:27:26,090
To get me fired again, I meant.

508
00:27:27,840 --> 00:27:29,110
Are you nuts?

509
00:27:29,250 --> 00:27:30,760
You were the one running off.

510
00:27:31,020 --> 00:27:32,310
I was just following you.

511
00:27:33,010 --> 00:27:34,020
Oh, yeah.

512
00:27:34,140 --> 00:27:34,880
You're right.

513
00:27:36,470 --> 00:27:37,740
You're not being smart again.

514
00:27:38,730 --> 00:27:39,840
You just insulted me again.

515
00:27:39,860 --> 00:27:41,520
You're always foul-mouthing me.

516
00:27:42,400 --> 00:27:43,720
You could say I'm insulting you.

517
00:27:44,120 --> 00:27:45,930
But if you give it some thought,

518
00:27:46,180 --> 00:27:48,140
I might just be helping you.

519
00:27:48,460 --> 00:27:49,270
Help with what?

520
00:27:49,860 --> 00:27:51,840
You were trying to get me fired back then.

521
00:28:02,380 --> 00:28:04,050
It's true that I wanted you out back then,

522
00:28:05,940 --> 00:28:07,610
but now, there's nowhere else
I want you to be.

523
00:28:13,110 --> 00:28:13,930
I like it...

524
00:28:18,170 --> 00:28:19,320
It's like playing with a cat.

525
00:28:24,570 --> 00:28:25,160
Uh...

526
00:28:25,180 --> 00:28:26,170
A cat.

527
00:28:26,220 --> 00:28:27,430
A real... cat.

528
00:28:27,740 --> 00:28:28,520
Meow.

529
00:28:28,540 --> 00:28:29,320
Meow...

530
00:28:34,690 --> 00:28:37,200
Did you just say I'm as cute as a cat?

531
00:28:42,350 --> 00:28:42,870
Mm...

532
00:28:42,890 --> 00:28:43,560
Mmm...

533
00:28:54,460 --> 00:28:55,250
What's that stance?

534
00:28:55,280 --> 00:28:55,840
Hilarious.

535
00:29:01,030 --> 00:29:01,920
Don't call me out!

536
00:29:09,410 --> 00:29:11,590
So you do have a clumsy side.

537
00:29:19,910 --> 00:29:20,800
I'm totally slick...

538
00:29:25,630 --> 00:29:26,560
That's true.

539
00:30:34,330 --> 00:30:35,900
Thank you for coming with me.

540
00:30:36,990 --> 00:30:37,670
Mm.

541
00:30:37,760 --> 00:30:39,020
Thank you, also,

542
00:30:39,590 --> 00:30:41,800
for helping me conquer a new territory.

543
00:30:43,550 --> 00:30:44,540
Conquer, huh?

544
00:30:45,340 --> 00:30:45,970
Mm.

545
00:30:46,300 --> 00:30:47,480
A bicycle ride?

546
00:30:47,760 --> 00:30:48,870
Well, I've never done that before,

547
00:30:49,530 --> 00:30:50,890
running off so suddenly.

548
00:30:51,610 --> 00:30:52,820
Good thing we finished working;

549
00:30:52,840 --> 00:30:54,130
otherwise, we'd be ditching work.

550
00:30:58,030 --> 00:30:59,440
Lower your head for me.

551
00:31:03,910 --> 00:31:04,770
Quick!

552
00:31:10,240 --> 00:31:11,480
Good job

553
00:31:11,530 --> 00:31:12,960
conquering it.

554
00:31:23,740 --> 00:31:24,920
You pet me like a dog.

555
00:31:25,990 --> 00:31:26,800
You're right.

556
00:31:27,300 --> 00:31:28,390
One with soft fur.

557
00:31:31,960 --> 00:31:33,450
This feels like a romantic scene, huh?

558
00:31:38,410 --> 00:31:39,630
In a series...

559
00:31:41,050 --> 00:31:42,910
the two male leads
have gotta kiss now, right?

560
00:31:48,080 --> 00:31:48,890
How?

561
00:31:55,480 --> 00:31:56,400
This is how.

562
00:32:13,620 --> 00:32:14,530
What a wuss.

563
00:32:23,140 --> 00:32:24,840
Still think I'm a wuss?

564
00:32:49,920 --> 00:32:50,960
There's a room available!

565
00:32:54,730 --> 00:32:56,190
Why don't you get a room already?

566
00:32:59,440 --> 00:33:00,960
Planning to tell the whole world?

567
00:33:03,100 --> 00:33:04,210
You're both fucking assholes.

568
00:33:13,830 --> 00:33:15,040
Are you gonna go explain yourself?

569
00:33:17,090 --> 00:33:17,980
No,

570
00:33:18,260 --> 00:33:19,400
I'm tired already.

571
